## 7) Negative result / anti-analysis note

Loading `libengine.so` out-of-context (extracted copy, `app_process` as uid 0/app uid) **fails**:

- `System.load()` → `UnsatisfiedLinkError: Attempt to load writable file` (writable-dir guard), and when loaded
  from `/data/local/tmp` the process **SIGSEGV**s inside the library: tombstone
  `#01 pc 00000000001243bc /data/local/tmp/…/libengine.so` → `#00 pc 0x76b7648b90 <unknown>` (jump to unmapped).
  i.e. the pack expects its real host context; the decrypted-code jump target only exists in the real process.
- `ilil/djp/...` then report `No implementation found … is the library loaded?` — they are **dynamically
  registered** (`RegisterNatives`), never `Java_com_snake_helper_Native_*` symbols. Confirms §1.

## 8) Tooling (no Frida anywhere)

| Tool | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `scripts/shizuku/MemScan.java` | scan `/proc/PID/mem` of a live process for patterns, dump hit regions |
| `scripts/shizuku/MemRegion.java` | full region dump (64-bit seek) + needle context + hexdump |
| `scripts/shizuku/PageStrings.java` | per-page string extraction of a dump (no `strings(1)` needed) |
| `scripts/shizuku/PtrFind.java` | find 64-bit pointers into a target address range (JNINativeMethod chase) |
| `scripts/shizuku/IlilDump.java` | live DEX reflection: enumerate `Native`/`vx` methods, invoke natives |
| `scripts/shizuku_call_ilil.sh` | end-to-end runner (compile → chunked push → run as app uid) |
